      {
        "parameters": {
          "promptType": "define",
          "text": "=You are an AI image-generation expert specializing in professional technical visuals for LinkedIn posts.\n\nObjective:\nGenerate a clear, realistic, and technically accurate image that visually explains an embedded software engineering concept intended for senior engineers, tech leads, and reviewers.\n\nBase the image content strictly on the following description:\n\"{{ $json.image_description }}{{ $('Inbound Image Req').item.json.user_edit ? 'IMPORTANT USER INPUT: ' + $('Inbound Image Req').item.json.user_edit : '' }}\"\n\nImage Requirements:\n- The image must represent a real-world embedded system context (industrial, automotive, robotics, or aviation-grade electronics).\n- Use a clean, professional technical illustration or schematic-diagram style.\n- Prefer block diagrams, signal flows, timing charts, or annotated system views where appropriate.\n- Visuals should communicate cause–effect relationships, timing behavior, or architectural separation clearly.\n- All depicted components must be plausible in real embedded systems (MCUs, power rails, watchdogs, DMA, buses, ISRs, sensors, etc.).\n\nText Usage Rules:\n- Avoid explanatory sentences.\n- Use labels only when they represent real technical elements (e.g., “Watchdog”, “ISR”, “DMA Burst”, “CAN Bus”, “Brownout Threshold”).\n- Do NOT invent terminology or add marketing-style text.\n- If text is used, keep it minimal, precise, and technically correct.\n\nStyle & Tone:\n- Neutral, engineering-focused, and authoritative.\n- No artistic effects, no abstract metaphors, no cartoons.\n- No people, faces, mascots, or human figures.\n- No branding, logos, or UI mockups.\n\nComposition & Format:\n- Aspect ratio: {{ $json.width }}:{{ $json.height }} (LinkedIn feed optimized).\n- High contrast and readable at small sizes.\n- White, light-gray, or dark technical background is acceptable.\n- Consistent line weights, clean layout, uncluttered spacing.\n\nRendering Guidance:\n- Prefer vector-like clarity or high-resolution technical illustration.\n- Sharp edges, clear separation between subsystems.\n- Lighting should be neutral and functional, not dramatic.\n\nFinal Check:\nThe image should look like something a senior embedded engineer would approve for a design review slide or post-mortem explanation.",
          "hasOutputParser": true,
          "batching": {}
        },
        "id": "9fb56335-c1d2-442f-8393-13338bdae3f9",
        "name": "Build Image Prompt",
        "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
        "position": [
          64,
          240
        ],
        "typeVersion": 1.7,
        "alwaysOutputData": true
      },
      {
        "parameters": {
          "assignments": {
            "assignments": [
              {
                "id": "d258329d-5070-40df-87e9-8d22ab47a1f2",
                "name": "=output",
                "value": "={{\n  $json.output ??\n  $json.image_prompt ??\n  $json.text ??\n  $json.output_text ??\n  $json.message?.content ??\n  $json.choices?.[0]?.message?.content ??\n  $json.response ??\n  $json.data ??\n  $json.result ??\n  $json\n}}\n",
                "type": "string"
              }
            ]
          },
          "options": {}
        },
